<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>NATHAN AI · UNBOXED · Original Source Recovery</title><meta name="theme-color" content="#091927"><link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css"><script src="core.js" defer></script><script src="app.js" defer></script></head><body>
<a class="skip" href="#find">Skip to search</a>
<header class="top"><a href="../../index.html">NATHAN AI</a><span>ONE MIND · ONE MASTER LIBRARY · UNBOXED</span><a href="../../app-factory/nathan-ai/hop-in/chatbox/">HOP IN Chatbox</a></header>
<main><section class="hero"><div class="eyebrow">RESTORE THE CONNECTIONS. NEVER REPLACE THE ORIGINALS.</div><h1>Everything stays<br><em>unboxed.</em></h1><p>No forced 14 boxes. No collapsed manuscripts. No guessed completion. Every recovered source retains its identity, original title, path, status, version reference and raw record when available. One original may appear in many searches without becoming many duplicate originals.</p>
<div class="metrics"><div><strong>19,317</strong><span>Owner catalog items · previously reconciled</span></div><div><strong>5,964</strong><span>Owner files · metadata snapshot</span></div><div><strong>7,918</strong><span>Language profiles · public registry</span></div><div><strong>1,023</strong><span>GitHub file paths · new tree snapshot</span></div></div>
<p class="fine">Different sources and count units overlap. The owner catalog's 19,317 underlying private originals are <strong>not</strong> included as files in the public GitHub repository. This screen loads public indexes and any originals you explicitly select, without uploading them.</p></section>
<section class="browse"><h2>Your open recovery table</h2><label for="find">Search across original names, paths, descriptions, identifiers and connected areas</label><input id="find" type="search" placeholder="paradox · primordial · ROOT · anomaly · nine cars · TORMO · book">
<div class="toolbar"><label for="collection">Source collection</label><select id="collection"><option value="">All loaded collections</option></select><label for="tag">Optional discovery tag</label><input id="tag" placeholder="Any word or theme; never changes originals"><button id="clear" type="button">Clear filters</button></div>
<div class="loaders" id="loaders"></div><p id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Choose a source collection to load. No private archive is accessed automatically.</p>
<div class="actions"><button id="more" type="button">Show more results</button><button id="export" type="button">Export current filtered metadata</button></div>
<div class="layout"><div><div class="summary"><span id="shown">No records loaded</span></div><div id="results" class="results"></div></div><aside id="detail" class="detail"><h3>Original record viewer</h3><p>Select a source. Its original record is shown separately from discovery labels.</p></aside></div></section>
<section class="local"><h2>Bring in the originals — privately</h2><p>Choose your owner catalog or recovery files. Accepts JSON, JSONL, CSV, TXT, Markdown, and source-code text; directory selection keeps individual file paths. Files stay in this browser tab. This does not publish, modify, overwrite, or transmit them.</p><label class="upload">Select original files <input id="files" type="file" multiple accept=".json,.jsonl,.csv,.tsv,.txt,.md,.js,.py,.html,.sql,.zip,.db,.sqlite"></label><label class="upload">Select an original folder <input id="folder" type="file" webkitdirectory directory multiple></label><p class="fine">ZIP and SQLite are indexed as original files, not unpacked or executed by this browser. Use the existing read-only archive inspector for member/row inspection. File sizes over 15 MB are indexed by name only; no silent truncation masquerades as full recovery. No local records are uploaded or placed into browser storage.</p><button id="drop-local" type="button">Clear only imported records from memory</button></section>
